    <statement><p>Find the integral</p>
<p><m>\int\, \left(z+1\right)e^{8z} dz =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(\frac{1+z}{8}-0.015625\right)e^{8z}+C</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\int\,u\,v'\,dx = u\cdot v - \int u'\,v\,dx</m>)
with <m>u = z+1</m> and <m>v' = e^{8 z}</m>, so
that <m>u' = 1</m> and <m>v = {1\over 8} e^{8 z}</m>.  Then
<me>\int\,\left(z+1\right)e^{8z}\,dz = 
  \frac{z+1}{8}\,e^{8 z} - \int\,{1\over 8} e^{8 z}\,dz =
  \frac{z+1}{8}\,e^{8 z} - {1\over 64} e^{8 z} + C.</me>



</solution>
